```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // The output type has no error channel, and under panic = "abort" any
        // panic becomes a wasm `unreachable` trap. An absent state key therefore
        // yields an empty list rather than a panic.
        let urls: Vec<String> = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not add `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`. This node's `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and I can't treat an unlisted grant as authority from the description alone. The enrichment call also can't be built as specified: `RunInfo` has no text field, so there is no `<the input's text>` to put in the query. If the grant is extended in the graph definition, the enrichment step can be added then, with a defined source for the query text.

